id:                     E3190
trigger_tool: 'test|runtime'
phase: 'testing|runtime'
error_signature: 'Unable to connect.*Name does not resolve|getaddrinfo.*EAI_NONAME.*(localhost\.local|\.local)'
severity:               2
category:               ohos, portability, testing, 'network, mdns'
match_keywords: 'localhost.local, .local, mDNS, mdns responder, avahi, nss-mdns, hostname, EAI_NONAME, Name does not resolve, loopback fallback'
title: 'Framework-qualified ".local" hostname cannot resolve on hosts without an mDNS responder (loopback fallback for self-connect tests)'
root_cause: >-
  Network frameworks qualify the bare auto-detected hostname with the ".local"
  mDNS domain by design (pappl appends ".local" in
  _papplSystemSetHostNameNoLock when no domain is present). Resolution of such
  names requires an mDNS responder plus nss-mdns; OHOS has neither, and the
  resolver falls through to unicast DNS which NXDOMAINs the name. Clients that
  connect to the system's own advertised hostname then fail with
  "Name does not resolve" even though the service listens on loopback.
affected_scope: >-
  Libraries that advertise themselves via DNS-SD and then let clients connect
  to the advertised hostname (pappl testpappl remote path: jpeg/png image
  tests). Bare-hostname connects ("localhost") resolve via /etc/hosts and are
  NOT affected - only the mDNS-qualified name is.
verification_cmd: >-
  Print the framework hostname: a papplSystemCreate + papplSystemGetHostName
  probe returns "localhost.local" on the device while gethostname() and
  gethostbyname() both return plain "localhost" (the qualification happens in
  library code, not libc). /etc/hosts has "127.0.0.1 localhost" but no
  localhost.local entry, and no mDNS responder is running.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: 'consumer-loopback-fallback'
rec_description: >-
  In the consumer or test harness, retry the connection against "localhost"
  when the advertised hostname fails to resolve; keep the library's mDNS
  naming convention untouched (it is correct where a responder exists).
rec_command: 'if ((http = httpConnect(host, ...)) == NULL && strcmp(host, "localhost")) { retry with "localhost"; }'
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: 'patch-testsuite-loopback-fallback'
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: 'explicit-sethostname'
fallback_description: >-
  Have the application pin a resolvable hostname at startup
  (papplSystemSetHostName(system, "localhost")). Note: a later reset to NULL
  re-introduces the qualified name, so the fallback in the connect path is
  more robust.
fallback_auto_fix: false
forbid_1_pattern: 'strip \.local|remove the .local suffix from DNS-SD names'
forbid_1_reason: 'The mDNS domain suffix is required for correct service advertisement on responder-equipped networks; stripping it fixes the test and breaks the feature.'
forbid_1_consequence: 'DNS-SD registration semantics change; on mDNS networks the service becomes unfindable.'
forbid_2_pattern: 'echo .* >> /etc/hosts|recipe writing hosts entries'
forbid_2_reason: '/etc/hosts needs root and the Conan recipe must not mutate system configuration.'
forbid_2_consequence: 'Build fails or the environment is silently mutated for every other package.'
source_event: 'pappl 1.4.12 on HarmonyOS PC: jpeg/png categories always failed with "Unable to connect: Name does not resolve" because papplSystemSetHostName(NULL) produced localhost.local; patch 0003 added the testsuite loopback fallback and the full -t all sweep (1821 cases incl. client-10x1000) then passed'
last_updated:               2026-10-19
authors:               frj__
doc_file:               doc/E3190.md
